Subject: [PATCH] turnip: do not require dedicated allocation for host imports

Host pointer imports carry no per-image metadata. Keep the existing dedicated
requirement for other external handle types, including mixed handle masks.
This does not change pitch, modifiers, UBWC, tiling or alias validation.

Apply after the pinned UniXNU Mesa patch stack. This is the narrow candidate
used by the Windows build; pandora-linear-dedicated.patch is an earlier, broader
proposal and must not be stacked with this patch.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -1169,8 +1169,14 @@ tu_get_image_memory_requirements(struct tu_device *dev, struct tu_image *image,
       case VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_MEMORY_DEDICATED_REQUIREMENTS: {
          VkMemoryDedicatedRequirements *req =
             (VkMemoryDedicatedRequirements *) ext;
+         /* Host pointer imports carry no per-image metadata, so an image
+          * over one may be bound at any offset of a shared import.
+          */
+         const VkExternalMemoryHandleTypeFlags host_types =
+            VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_HOST_ALLOCATION_BIT_EXT |
+            VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_HOST_MAPPED_FOREIGN_MEMORY_BIT_EXT;
          req->requiresDedicatedAllocation =
-            image->vk.external_handle_types != 0;
+            (image->vk.external_handle_types & ~host_types) != 0;
          req->prefersDedicatedAllocation = req->requiresDedicatedAllocation;
          break;
       }
